<title>FRANCE: French sugar producers raise 96/97 output estimate.</title>
<headline>French sugar producers raise 96/97 output estimate.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>French sugar producers said on Wednesday they had raised their estimate for 1996/97 beet sugar output to 4.05 million tonnes from a previous target of four million.</p>
<p>The estimate matched the forecast issued last week by French sugar intervention board FIRS, a spokeswoman for the SNFS sugar manufacturers' association told Reuters.</p>
<p>The new estimate was based on data collected by beet processing plants up until this week, she said.</p>
<p>But the new figure would still represent a decline from the 4.199 million tonnes of beet sugar produced in 1995/96.</p>
</text>
